          "scene_003": {
            "scene_id": "scene_003",
            "heading": "INT. DRE'S APARTMENT \u2014 NIGHTMaya visits Dre. He doesn't know what she knows. To him, everything is still normal.",
            "location": "DRE'S APARTMENT \u2014 NIGHTMaya visits Dre. He doesn't know what she knows. To him, everything is still normal.",
            "time_of_day": "",
            "characters": [
              "DRE",
              "MAYA"
            ],
            "text": "He's cooking. Music playing. The apartment feels lived-in, warm.\nShe watches him from the doorway before he notices her.\nMAYA (V.O.)\nThis is the version of him I want to remember. The\none who used to split his last twenty dollars with me at\nthe gas station. The one who showed up when I\nneeded him. That person was real. I have to believe\nthat.\nDre turns and sees her.\nDRE\nYou good? You're looking at me weird.\nMAYA\nI'm fine. Just tired.\nDRE\nYou eat?\nMAYA\nYeah.\nHe puts a plate in front of her anyway. She looks down at it. She knows that in two\nmonths this apartment will be stripped bare. She knows what hunger will do to him.\nMAYA\nHey. If something happened \u2014 something bad \u2014\nyou'd tell me, right?\nDRE\nWhat kind of something?\nMAYA\nI don't know. Anything. Would you come to me?\nDRE\n(beat, easy smile)\nMaya. You're my people. Always.\nShe nods. She almost believes him.\nTHE COUNTDOWN\nMaya creates a survival blueprint. Food. Water. Power. Medical. Security. People.\nShe writes two lists.\nThe first list: names of people she will save.\nThe second list: names she cannot. Dre's name is not on either list yet.She stares at both lists for a long time. Then she folds them and puts them away.\nTHE HOMESTEAD\nEXT./INT. ABANDONED HIGH RISE, DOWNTOWN CHICAGO \u2014 DAY\nMaya finds an abandoned high rise in Downtown Chicago. A building everyone forgot.\nShe sees a future inside it. She transforms it into a survival sanctuary.\nThe rooftop becomes a farm. Hydroponics. Seeds. Rain collection. Winter preparation.\nThe building gets solar power, batteries, generators, storage rooms, a medical area,\nsecurity systems, and emergency exits.\nMAYA (V.O.)\nI'm not preparing for monsters. I'm preparing for\npeople. People are always the hardest part.\nSUPPLIES\nMaya collects supplies before the world knows it needs them. Food. Water filters.\nMedicine. Tools. Seeds. Preservation equipment. Repair materials.\nShe learns how to maintain everything. Every decision matters because she knows\ntime is running out.\nTHE SUPPLY RUN \u2014 WHAT GOES WRONG",
            "description": "He's cooking. Music playing. The apartment feels lived-in, warm.\nShe watches him from the doorway before he notices her.\nMAYA (V.O.)\nThis is the version of him I want to remember. The\none who used to split his last twenty dollars with me at\nthe gas station. The one who showed up when I\nneeded him. That person was real. I have to believe\nthat.\nDre turns and sees her.\nDRE\nYou good? You're looking at me weird.\nMAYA\nI'm fine. Just tired.\nDRE\nYou eat?\nMAYA\nYeah.\nHe puts a plate in front of her anyway. She looks down at it. She knows that in two\nmonths this apartment will be stripped bare. She knows what hunger will do to him.\nMAYA\nHey. If something happened \u2014 something bad \u2014\nyou'd tell me, right?\nDRE\nWhat kind of something?\nMAYA\nI don't know. Anything. Would you come to me?\nDRE\n(beat, easy smile)\nMaya. You're my people. Always.\nShe nods. She almost believes him.\nTHE COUNTDOWN\nMaya creates a survival blueprint. Food. Water. Power. Medical. Security. People.\nShe writes two lists.\nThe first list: names of people she will save.\nThe second list: names she cannot. Dre's name is not on either list yet.She stares at both lists for a long time. Then she folds them and puts them away.\nTHE HOMESTEAD\nEXT./INT. ABANDONED HIGH RISE, DOWNTOWN CHICAGO \u2014 DAY\nMaya finds an abandoned high rise in Downtown Chicago. A building everyone forgot.\nShe sees a future inside it. She transforms it into a survival sanctuary.\nThe rooftop becomes a farm. Hydroponics. Seeds. Rain collection. Winter preparation.\nThe building gets solar power, batteries, generators, storage rooms, a medical area,\nsecurity systems, and emergency exits.\nMAYA (V.O.)\nI'm not preparing for monsters. I'm preparing for\npeople. People are always the hardest part.\nSUPPLIES\nMaya collects supplies before the world knows it needs them. Food. Water filters.\nMedicine. Tools. Seeds. Preservation equipment. Repair materials.\nShe learns how to maintain everything. Every decision matters because she knows\ntime is running out.\nTHE SUPPLY RUN \u2014 WHAT GOES WRONG",
