            "text": "Maya stands on the rooftop. Chicago is dark. Her building glows. Plants move in the\nwind. A small piece of humanity survives.\nBelow, she can hear voices. Her mother. Jay. Simone. Elena. People living.\nMAYA (V.O.)\nThe first time the world ended, I lost everything.\nMAYA (V.O.) (CONT'D)\nThe second time, I prepared.\nMAYA (V.O.) (CONT'D)\nI thought being reborn meant getting revenge. I was\nwrong.\nMAYA (V.O.) (CONT'D)\nIt meant I finally had the power to choose what\nsurvived.\nShe looks out at the dark city. At the stars finally visible without the light pollution.\nMAYA (V.O.) (CONT'D)\nThe nightmare showed me who we became. The\nsecond chance showed me who we could be instead.\nI chose that version. Every single day, I chose it.\nFADE TO BLACK.FADE OUT.",
